// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// An inline embedded property mapping is spelled `prop() Inline [id]` -- with an EMPTY pair
// of parentheses that carries no content and is not optional. The rule is literally
// `PAREN_OPEN PAREN_CLOSE INLINE BRACKET_OPEN identifier BRACKET_CLOSE`.
//
// The parens exist only to make this arm distinguishable from an ordinary embedded mapping,
// so they look like noise and are the obvious thing for a rewrite to make optional. Note
// also that the id in brackets is a plain identifier, not a qualified name.
###Mapping
Mapping fixture::neg::InlineNoParens
(
   fixture::neg::Firm: Relational
   {
      ~mainTable [fixture::neg::Db]FIRM
      legalName: [fixture::neg::Db]FIRM.LEGAL_NAME,
      employees Inline [personMapping]
   }
)
